hyperactive-interaction-in-the-words-of-the-human-superorganism-24 = unlines (cons (quoted (cons "Since a computer is a counter and a teller, computing was always narration. The difference in hyperactivity is that the narration keeps its witnesses. *History* is Greek *historia*, inquiry, from *histōr*, the one who knows because they saw, the witness. *Witness*, *wit*, *wise*, *vision*, *evidence*, *video* and Greek *idea*, the form seen, all come from the root for " (cons "to see, to know" (cons ". History is witnessing kept. A proof in type theory is called a witness. Keeping every historical binding in the store is keeping witnesses. When the specializer carries a proof of its rewrite, the computation recounts itself with its witness attached. Witnessed computation is history in the oldest sense: what was seen, kept, and able to testify." nil)))) nil)
